From: Tomato64 <noreply@tomato64>
Subject: [PATCH] terminate the variadic argument list in d_printf()

d_printf() calls va_start() without a matching va_end(). The pairing is
required by the C standard, and on the ABIs where va_end() is not a no-op
this leaves the argument list unterminated on every log line.

diff --git a/common.c b/common.c
index 018ec86..055bd0a 100644
--- a/common.c
+++ b/common.c
@@ -3373,6 +3373,7 @@ d_printf(int level, const char *fname, const char *fmt, ...)
 
 	va_start(ap, fmt);
 	vsnprintf(logbuf, sizeof(logbuf), fmt, ap);
+	va_end(ap);
 
 	if (*fname == '\0')
 		printfname = 0;
